  "derivation_definition": [
    "Complete raw attempts were copied byte-for-byte to a private archive outside the repository; the archive is not published and its local path is intentionally omitted.",
    "Public command records replace absolute helper/build/output paths with relative helper paths and FIRST_BUILD, SECOND_BUILD, SOURCE_SHA, VERSION, and OUTPUT placeholders.",
    "Path-bearing hash files retain each digest and replace path labels with basenames or a relative helper label.",
    "Original helper source copies are retained byte-for-byte with a .go.txt suffix; the replay command copies the archived source to a transient .go file before go run so it is not discovered as a package source.",
    "stdout/stderr are byte-exact where they contain no local paths; transformations and original/derived hashes are listed per file."
  ],
